Z||000002||Old Lar||11-25-2000||04:41 PM||||It's your personal choice.  My opinion worth $0.02 is the dark grey with the light grey inserts.  Or even light grey/light grey to keep it looking like the stock.  Unless there is lots of red in the car or the interior is customized, I'd stay away from the red inserts.   Unless you had an Indy Pace car.||||reg||3
Z||000003||Seanh||11-26-2000||09:40 AM||||Yeah, I was kinda thinking that. I just really like red, alot. Like I said before, the only red in the interior is the steering wheel. I am going to have a leather wrapped dash and door panels, but they will be light gray. I really dont like the dark gray interior that was in the 86's. I would rather have an light Gray interior, so thats what I am going to do with the leather on the door panels and dash. I dont know yet, but I might try building my own dash. I found one I really liked, but it $2,000! I cant see paying that for a fancy dash that was hand built. Oh well, I'll find somthing I like some day.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I am thinking Dark Gray w/lite Gray inserts now. I like that idea.||||reg||1
